{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Fall 2026 CS2 \u2014 Semester Topic Map\n\nTeaching story: earn a trustworthy boundary, then make it collaborate, substitute, swap, hold data, explain tradeoffs, respond to events, and tell an honest evidence-backed story.\n\nArrows labeled documented follow the active sequence; arrows labeled inferred (orange) are instructional synthesis. Testing, documentation, AI accountability, and review recur throughout (S08).",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 1580,
      "height": 186
    },
    {
      "id": "spine",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Progression\nWeeks 3\u20134 design \u2192 5 substitution \u2192 6 contracts \u2192 7\u20138 data abstractions and search/order \u2192 9 GUI/events \u2192 10\u201311 visualization/storytelling. Recursion is an optional design lens when authentic.\n\nSource: docs/curriculum/course-sequence.md:15-22",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 236,
      "width": 1580,
      "height": 173
    },
    {
      "id": "phase1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Phase 1 \u00b7 Design a boundary",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 509,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 82
    },
    {
      "id": "g1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 1 \u00b7 Earn a boundary\nWeeks 3\u20134 \u00b7 S01\n\nWhy it matters: state and behavior should make a small promise that can be explained and tested. Predictions may be rejected.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-04.md; lessons/week-04-cohesive-object-boundary.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-04.md",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 641,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 342
    },
    {
      "id": "g2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 2 \u00b7 Collaborate and protect\nWeek 4\u20135 \u00b7 S01/S08\n\nWhy it matters: composition gives responsibilities a boundary; an invariant makes correctness observable.\n\nEvidence: lessons/week-04-composition-and-invariants.md; planning/week-05.md",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1083,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 316
    },
    {
      "id": "g3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 3 \u00b7 Earn substitution\nWeek 6 \u00b7 S02\n\nWhy it matters: inheritance is used only when a genuine is-a relationship gives shared operations different meaning.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-06.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-06.md; week_06/03_test_substitution.py",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1499,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 316
    },
    {
      "id": "phase2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Phase 2 \u00b7 Contracts and data",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 509,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 82
    },
    {
      "id": "g4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 4 \u00b7 Make a contract swappable\nWeek 7 \u00b7 S03/S08\n\nWhy it matters: a caller can depend on a promise while implementations change.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-07.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-07.md; week_07/week_07_contract_and_swap/",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 641,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 316
    },
    {
      "id": "g5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 5 \u00b7 Choose a world-fit data shape\nWeek 8 \u00b7 S05\n\nWhy it matters: list/stack/queue behavior becomes meaningful when chosen for a real process and proved with a trace or test.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-08.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-08.md",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 1057,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 328
    },
    {
      "id": "g6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 6 \u00b7 Explain lookup/order tradeoffs\nWeek 9 \u00b7 S05/S06\n\nWhy it matters: algorithm choice follows domain need, maintenance cost, and preconditions; binary search is conditional.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-09.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-09.md; lessons/plotting-searching-sorting.md",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 1485,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 380
    },
    {
      "id": "phase3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Phase 3 \u00b7 Events and story",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 509,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 82
    },
    {
      "id": "g7",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 7 \u00b7 Put a thin view over the model\nWeek 10 \u00b7 S04\n\nWhy it matters: an event can change real model state without making the GUI the only proof.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-10.md; lessons/week-10-tkinter-model-view-lab.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-10.md",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 641,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 354
    },
    {
      "id": "g8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 8 \u00b7 Turn project data into a story\nWeeks 11\u201312 \u00b7 S09/S07\n\nWhy it matters: a question, readable representation, limitation, and decision make evidence useful; recursion/linked/nested design is optional when authentic.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-11.md; planning/week-12.md; lessons/week-11-data-storytelling-micro-lab.md; assignments/odyssey_gates/week-11.md and week-12.md",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 1095,
      "width": 340,
      "height": 432
    },
    {
      "id": "evidence",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Recurring proof loop (Weeks 2\u201315 \u00b7 S08)\nKnown baseline \u2192 bounded change \u2192 inspect diff/code \u2192 independent test or trace \u2192 explain limits \u2192 accept/reject and review. This loop applies to every card above; it is not an arrow because it recurs everywhere.\n\nEvidence: planning/week-02.md; docs/curriculum/course-sequence.md:22; later Odyssey gates.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1965,
      "width": 1580,
      "height": 173
    },
    {
